From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:16:15 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] create standard /var symlinks in the image (modules/rootfs)

The generated Mobile-NixOS rootfs image did not contain /var/run or /var/lock, so stage-1 and tmpfiles workarounds were needed. Create the standard symlinks in populateCommands so every boot sees them before early systemd units.
---
 modules/rootfs.nix | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/rootfs.nix b/modules/rootfs.nix
index 0af0c136..718c1b2d 100644
--- a/modules/rootfs.nix
+++ b/modules/rootfs.nix
@@ -49,6 +49,11 @@ in
       in
       ''
         mkdir -p ./nix/store
+        # The generated rootfs must contain the standard /var symlinks before
+        # systemd starts; creating them in stage 1 is too late for early units.
+        mkdir -p ./var
+        ln -sfn /run ./var/run
+        ln -sfn /run/lock ./var/lock
         echo "Copying system closure..."
 
         err=0
@@ -69,6 +74,15 @@ in
 
         echo "Done copying system closure..."
         cp -v ${closureInfo}/registration ./nix-path-registration
+
+        # The image builder runs unprivileged, so the root of the filesystem and
+        # the directories created above would otherwise be owned by uid 1000,
+        # which is ceres on the device. systemd-tmpfiles then refuses to create
+        # symlinks such as the compositor environment file across the unsafe
+        # ownership transition, leaving the launcher without QPA_HWC_FORCE_GLES
+        # and QPA_HWC2_FORCE_DOZE_UPDATE.
+        chown -h 0:0 . ./*
+        chown -R 0:0 ./nix/store
       '';
 
       # Give some headroom for initial mounting.
